From: surface-kit
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: pipeline: simple: Cancel unconverted output buffers on capture errors

When a capture buffer completes with an error and the software ISP or a
converter is in use, imageBufferReady() completes the request with its
user-facing output buffers without converting anything into them. Their
metadata is left as it was, so they come back to the application as
successful frames holding the image and timestamp of whatever frame last
went through that buffer.

On a camera with an intermittently failing CSI-2 link (Surface Pro 7 front
ov5693 on IPU4) this shows up as the picture jumping back in time every
few dozen frames, with sensor timestamps going backwards.

Cancel the output buffers before completing them, which also marks the
request as cancelled, so applications drop the frame.

---
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -40,6 +40,7 @@
 #include "libcamera/internal/delayed_controls.h"
 #include "libcamera/internal/device_enumerator.h"
 #include "libcamera/internal/formats.h"
+#include "libcamera/internal/framebuffer.h"
 #include "libcamera/internal/global_configuration.h"
 #include "libcamera/internal/media_device.h"
 #include "libcamera/internal/pipeline_handler.h"
@@ -908,8 +909,16 @@
 			return;
 
 		const RequestOutputs &outputs = conversionQueue_.front();
-		for (auto &[stream, buf] : outputs.outputs)
+		for (auto &[stream, buf] : outputs.outputs) {
+			/*
+			 * The output buffer was never written for this frame and
+			 * still holds the image (and metadata) of whatever frame
+			 * last went through it. Cancel it so applications don't
+			 * display a stale frame as a new one.
+			 */
+			buf->_d()->cancel();
 			pipe->completeBuffer(outputs.request, buf);
+		}
 		SimpleFrameInfo *info = frameInfo_.find(outputs.request->sequence());
 		if (info)
 			info->metadataRequired = false;
